# Grafana Alloy Docker Example (Grafana Cloud)

New scenarios send telemetry to **Grafana Cloud**. Do not add Loki, Prometheus, Tempo, Grafana, or Pyroscope services.

Read [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) and [`_cloud/README.md`](../_cloud/README.md) first.

## Directory structure

```
your-example-name/
├── pipeline.alloy          # Fleet paste (no destinations). Omit if a Fleet integration template exists.
├── config.alloy            # Compose lab only; imports _cloud/destinations.alloy
├── docker-compose.yml      # Optional synthetic workload
├── README.md               # Fleet click-path first; Compose last
└── [additional files...]
```

Customer path is Fleet template or `pipeline.alloy`. Do not tell them to run Compose unless they have no collector.

## README

Lead with Fleet: integration template, or paste `pipeline.alloy`. `config.alloy` is SE practice. Include YAML frontmatter: `os`, `signals`, `deploy`, `cloud_products`. Verify with `gcx fleet collectors list` plus `gcx metrics query` / `gcx logs query`. Visualization is `GC_GRAFANA_URL`. Add the scenario to `_cloud/pov-index.yaml` and the root README.

## docker-compose.yml

```yaml
services:
  # Demo workload(s) here

  alloy:
    image: grafana/alloy:${GRAFANA_ALLOY_VERSION:-v1.17.1}
    ports:
      - 12345:12345
    env_file:
      - ../.env
    environment:
      GC_DESTINATIONS_FILE: /etc/alloy/cloud/destinations.alloy
    volumes:
      - ./config.alloy:/etc/alloy/config.alloy
      - ../_cloud/destinations.alloy:/etc/alloy/cloud/destinations.alloy
    command: run --server.http.listen-addr=0.0.0.0:12345 --storage.path=/var/lib/alloy/data /etc/alloy/config.alloy
```

## config.alloy

Instantiate only the signals you use.

```river
import.file "grafana_cloud" {
  filename = sys.env("GC_DESTINATIONS_FILE")
}

livedebugging {
  enabled = true
}

grafana_cloud.metrics "default" {}
grafana_cloud.logs "default" {}
grafana_cloud.otlp "default" {}
grafana_cloud.profiles "default" {}

// Example: scrape → Cloud metrics
prometheus.scrape "example" {
  targets    = [{"__address__" = "app:8080"}]
  forward_to = [grafana_cloud.metrics.default.receiver]
  job_name   = "integrations/example"
  scrape_interval = "1m" // Grafana Cloud 1 DPM; 15s is 4x billed series traffic
}

// Example: OTLP traces → Cloud
otelcol.receiver.otlp "default" {
  http {}
  grpc {}
  output {
    traces = [otelcol.processor.batch.default.input]
  }
}

otelcol.processor.batch "default" {
  output {
    traces = [grafana_cloud.otlp.default.input]
  }
}
```

Align `job` with Grafana Cloud integration names when an integration exists (`integrations/postgres_exporter`, `integrations/node_exporter`, …). Compose `config.alloy` is SE practice; customer paste is `pipeline.alloy`.

Windows: `.\run-example.ps1 your-example-name` (lab only)  
Linux: `./run-example.sh your-example-name`
